# Rosemarry Engineering Standards & Git Workflow

This document defines the coding standards, project structure, development practices, and Git workflow for the Rosemarry project.

---

# 1. Technology Stack

| Area                 | Technology                   |
| -------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Mobile               | React Native                 |
| Mobile Framework     | Expo                         |
| Language             | TypeScript                   |
| Routing              | Expo Router                  |
| Backend              | Node.js + TypeScript         |
| API                  | REST                         |
| Database             | PostgreSQL 16                |
| Database Access      | Raw SQL with `pg`            |
| Local Infrastructure | Docker                       |
| Media Storage        | Object storage               |
| Cache                | Redis when required          |
| AI / ML              | Python service when required |

---

# 2. Engineering Priorities

Code should prioritise:

| Priority        | Description                                    |
| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| Correctness     | Code should behave as expected                 |
| Security        | User and system data must be protected         |
| Maintainability | Code should be easy to update                  |
| Readability     | Code should be easy to understand              |
| Performance     | Avoid unnecessary processing and database work |
| Simplicity      | Avoid unnecessary abstractions and services    |

---

# 3. TypeScript Standards

Avoid `any`.

```ts
interface CreateUserInput {
  email: string;
  password: string;
}

function createUser(data: CreateUserInput) {
  // implementation
}
```

Use explicit types where they improve safety and readability.

---

# 4. Naming Standards

| Item       | Convention         | Example              |
| ---------- | ------------------ | -------------------- |
| Variables  | `camelCase`        | `userId`             |
| Functions  | `camelCase`        | `findUserByEmail()`  |
| Interfaces | `PascalCase`       | `CreateUserInput`    |
| Types      | `PascalCase`       | `AccountStatus`      |
| Classes    | `PascalCase`       | `AuthService`        |
| Constants  | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `MAX_PROFILE_PHOTOS` |
| Files      | lowercase          | `auth.service.ts`    |


# 5. Database Standards

PostgreSQL is the primary database.

Use parameterised queries.

example:
```ts
const result = await pool.query(
  `
    SELECT
      user_id,
      email,
      account_status,
      user_role
    FROM users
    WHERE email = $1 --> never expose actual email
  `,
  [email], 
);
```

Database integrity should use (DDL):

| Feature           | Purpose                     |
| ----------------- | --------------------------- |
| Primary Key       | Uniquely identifies records |
| Foreign Key       | Maintains relationships     |
| Unique Constraint | Prevents duplicate values   |
| Check Constraint  | Enforces valid values       |
| Index             | Improves query performance  |
| Transaction       | Groups dependent operations |

---

# 6. Database Migrations

Schema changes must use migrations.

```text
database/
├── migrations/
│   ├── 001_create_users.sql
│   ├── 002_create_profiles.sql
│   ├── 003_create_matches.sql
│   └── 004_create_groups.sql
└── seeds/
```

Rules:

| Rule                        | Standard                     |
| --------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Production schema changes   | Use migrations               |
| Existing deployed migration | Do not modify                |
| New schema change           | Create a new migration       |
| Feature requiring DB change | Include migration in same PR |

---

# 7. Request Validation

Validate all external input.

This includes:

* Request body
* Query parameters
* Route parameters
* File uploads
* External API responses
* Webhooks

Example:

```ts
const registerSchema = z.object({
  email: z.string().email(),
  password: z.string().min(8),
});
```

Validation should happen before business logic.

---

# 8. Error Handling

Use centralised error handling.

| Error Type              | Example Status |
| ----------------------- | -------------: |
| Invalid input           |          `400` |
| Authentication required |          `401` |
| Permission denied       |          `403` |
| Resource not found      |          `404` |
| Conflict                |          `409` |
| Rate limit              |          `429` |
| Server error            |          `500` |

Internal stack traces and database errors should not be returned to the client.

---

# 9. API Standards

API endpoints should be versioned.

```text
/api/v1/auth
/api/v1/users
/api/v1/profiles
/api/v1/discovery
/api/v1/groups
/api/v1/matches
/api/v1/messages
```

Use standard HTTP methods.

| Method   | Purpose        |
| -------- | -------------- |
| `GET`    | Read           |
| `POST`   | Create         |
| `PATCH`  | Partial update |
| `PUT`    | Replace        |
| `DELETE` | Delete         |


